      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early settlers arrived in the late 1850s, with families like the Lathums and Couches moving near Deer Creek around 1858‑59.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/fredonia-tx-mason-county",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1874 the community built Hayes and Lathum School, and a church and school building followed the next year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/fredonia-tx-mason-county",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A short‑lived local paper, the Fredonia Kicker, was published from Robertson’s home for a brief period.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
